 r←key AddDependencyTarget(value target);msg;folder;oldTarget
⍝ Returns the "tatin" or "nuget" dependency setting `value` with the target namespace `target` added.
⍝ `key` names the setting, e.g. 'dependencies_dev.tatin'; it is used in messages only.
⍝ Signals an error when `value` is invalid, defines no folder or has a target namespace already,
⍝ and when `target` is not a valid target namespace.
 (msg folder oldTarget)←key ParseDependencySetting value
 msg Assert 0=≢msg
 ('No folder is defined in "',key,'"; cannot add a target namespace')Assert 0<≢folder
 ('There is already a target namespace defined in "',key,'"; edit the project config file to change that')Assert 0=≢oldTarget
 r←ComposeDependencySetting folder target
 msg←⊃key ParseDependencySetting r
 msg Assert 0=≢msg
⍝Done
